# Panic-by-default on the COMBINATOR `unwrap_error` lowering (reference §15.2).
#
# A module-level static receiver is a `Constant::GlobalRef` — NOT a Copy/Move
# place — so the GIR fast-path (`__result_unwrap_error` → the LIR Tier-2a tag
# guard) does not fire; the call survives to the backends as a monomorphized
# `Result__int64_t__int64_t__unwrap_error` CallExtern handled by each backend's
# inline combinator arm. D11 normalizes this to trap[T_UnwrapErrorOnOk] +
# exit 101 on BOTH backends (the LLVM lane shipped this arm with NO tag guard —
# an Ok receiver silently kept running with a garbage payload load).
Result[int, int] R = Ok(7)

void main():
    print("before")
    R.unwrap_error()
    print("unreachable")
